.TH PUMP 1 "September 2026" "Data Pump 001_00" "User Commands"
.nh
.ad l
.nr HY 0
.ds AD l
.SH NAME
pump \- transfer text and files over audio
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pump
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B pump
.BR \-\-help " | " \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pump
sends and receives text, files and exact bit strings through an audio device
or a WAV file. It also simulates links, estimates airtime and produces QR images.
The desktop interface is
.BR datapump-gui (1).
.PP
Both ends must use matching modem, source compression, error correction and
key settings. Bandwidth is not the payload bit rate. Use
.B estimate
before sending at a slow setting.
.PP
This page describes the regular modem. The independent Fast commands and their
options are documented in
.BR pump-fast (1).
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B tx
Send text or a file. Requires
.B \-\-output
for a WAV file or
.B \-\-device
for live audio; choose one.
.TP
.B rx
Decode a WAV selected by
.BR \-\-input ,
or record an audio device for
.B \-\-seconds
and decode the recording. Use
.B \-\-save
to write recovered source bytes.
.TP
.B listen
Receive continuously from the default audio device, or the selected
.BR \-\-device .
Stop with Ctrl-C or set
.BR \-\-seconds .
With
.B \-\-text
or
.BR \-\-input ,
also transmit one message. A simulation preset selects a simulated channel.
.TP
.B simulate
Transmit through a sampled channel and attempt blind reception. No audio device
is used. Optionally save the simulated capture with
.BR \-\-output .
.TP
.B estimate
Print JSON containing encoded size, wire bits, airtime, modem settings and a
relative low-probability-of-intercept model. Does not generate audio.
Model estimates do not establish physical-link performance or secrecy.
.TP
.B analyze-link
Print statistical link analysis as JSON. Requires
.BR \-\-text ,
.B \-\-input
or
.BR \-\-bits ,
and either a simulation preset or both
.B \-\-tx\-dbm
and
.BR \-\-attenuation\-db .
Does not generate audio or run the receiver.
.TP
.B status-tx
Send the exact 1\(en4096 binary digits given by
.BR \-\-bits .
Requires a WAV output or audio device. Leading zeros and partial bytes are
significant; no header, padding, error correction or authentication is added.
.TP
.B status-rx
Discover raw bits in a WAV, then compare them with
.BR \-\-bits .
Always prints JSON. The expected bits do not guide acquisition; a match is
not authentication.
.TP
.B devices
List audio device identifiers and descriptions, separated by tabs.
.TP
.B keygen
Create a symmetric keyfile at
.BR \-\-output .
The file contains a 128 MiB random header and an encrypted named key collection.
It is created with owner-only access and must not already exist.
.TP
.B keys
List the names in
.BR \-\-keyfile ,
one per line.
.TP
.B qr
Encode UTF-8 input as a QR Level L image, up to 500 Unicode characters.
Writes SVG by default, to standard output or
.BR \-\-output .
QR input is plaintext; key and audio options do not apply.
.TP
.BR fast-info ", " fast-tx ", " fast-rx ", " fast-listen
Inspect, send or receive with the independent Fast modem. See
.BR pump-fast (1).
.SH OPTIONS
Options take the form
.BI \-\-name " value"
or
.BI \-\-name= value .
Flags take no value. Duplicate and unknown options are errors.
.SS Input and output
.TP
.BI \-\-text " text"
Text to send. Mutually exclusive with
.BR \-\-input .
.TP
.BI \-\-input " path"
Source file for transmission, or WAV for reception. A single
.B \-
reads standard input. Transmit commands without
.B \-\-text
or
.B \-\-input
read standard input.
.TP
.BI \-\-kind " text|file|screenshot"
Source kind. Defaults to text for
.B \-\-text
or standard input, and file for a named input path.
.TP
.BI \-\-filename " name"
Display filename for an attachment; a basename, not a destination path.
Defaults to the input basename.
.TP
.BI \-\-output " path"
Create a WAV, keyfile or QR image. Existing files are never overwritten.
.TP
.BI \-\-save " path"
For
.B rx
only: save exact decoded source bytes after physical completion.
Fails if there is no complete decoded source or the path already exists.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print received content and diagnostics as JSON. See
.B OUTPUT
for completion and event handling.
.TP
.BI \-\-callsign " text"
.TQ
.BI \-\-grid " text"
Set local callsign and grid metadata. These fields are not transmitted;
include them in the text to send them.
.TP
.B \-\-repeatable
Apply the local repeatable-text eligibility limit: two seconds of wire-bit
airtime, with a one-byte minimum allowance. This flag is not transmitted
and does not start a repeating transmit loop.
.TP
.BI \-\-bits " digits"
Exact binary input for the status commands or
.BR analyze-link .
Only
.B 0
and
.B 1
are allowed; length is 1\(en4096.
.TP
.BI \-\-format " svg|pbm"
QR image format; default
.BR svg .
.SS Modem and reception
.TP
.BI \-\-bw " Hz"
Nominal bandwidth, 0.001\(en30000000 Hz; default 1200.
Decimal values and suffixes
.BR Hz ,
.BR k ,
.B kHz
and
.B MHz
are accepted. The usable audio-device passband still applies.
.TP
.BI \-\-target\-snr " dB-Hz"
Transmit planning target C/N0; default 32. Selects automatic tuning.
This is a configured target, not a measured signal-to-noise ratio.
.TP
.BI \-\-receive\-targets " list"
Comma-separated receive C/N0 targets; default 32. Requires automatic tuning.
Invalid lists reset to 32 with a diagnostic. Bandwidth and pattern stay fixed.
For example:
.BR "40,6,\-6" .
.TP
.BI \-\-pattern " mode"
Select automatic tuning with
.BR auto-keystream ,
.B auto-pattern
or
.BR auto-tone ;
or select
.BI pattern- N
with N = 3, 4, 6, 8, 12, 16, or
.BI tone- N
with N = 1, 2, 3, 4, 8, 32, 128, 1024, 4096, 16384.
Defaults to auto-keystream with a keyfile, auto-pattern otherwise.
Tone modes disable encryption and private spreading.
.TP
.BI \-\-sample\-rate " Hz"
Manual internal DSP clock, 64\(en120000000 samples/second.
Normally chosen from bandwidth and the real stream tone (Carrier minus Shift),
at least four times each.
The usual 1200 Hz bandwidth, Carrier 1500 Hz and Shift 0 use 6000 samples/second.
Audio hardware negotiates its own clock and resamples as needed.
.TP
.BI \-\-carrier " FREQUENCY"
Absolute transmitted/received carrier. At Shift 0, the default is the greater
of 1500 Hz and 0.75 times bandwidth. Works with automatic planning.
Carrier minus Shift must be positive and at most 30 MHz for the real USB stream.
Case-insensitive Hz, kHz, MHz, GHz and THz suffixes, k/m/g/t shorthand, optional
spaces and scientific notation are accepted; a plain number is in Hz.
.B \-\-rf\-carrier
is an alias; matching carrier aliases may be combined.
.TP
.BI \-\-shift " FREQUENCY"
Nonnegative RF translation or LO; default 0.
Accepts the same frequency units as Carrier.
Carrier 1001500 and Shift 1000000 give a real 1500 Hz tone; at Shift 0 the same
Carrier requires direct MHz-capable real samples.
.B \-\-rf\-shift
is an alias; choose one shift spelling.
USB is fixed; \-\-sideband upper is a compatibility no-op and lower is rejected.
No hardware tuning or external complex I/Q interface is added.
.TP
.BI \-\-spreading " N"
Manual chips per symbol, 1\(en16384.
.TP
.B \-\-scramble
Enable keyed pattern rotation. Requires a keyfile.
.TP
.B \-\-dsss
Enable independent keyed direct-sequence spreading. Requires a keyfile.
.PP
Any manual sample-rate, spreading, scramble or DSSS option disables
automatic tuning. These options cannot be combined with
.B \-\-target\-snr
or
.BR \-\-pattern .
.TP
.BI \-\-fec " 20|60|off"
Reed\(enSolomon parity overhead for interval sources; default 60.
Does not add parity to short text or exact bit strings.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-compression
Disable interval source compression. Both peers must select the same codec.
The fixed short-text dictionary is unchanged.
.TP
.BI \-\-time " seconds"
Local UNIX epoch in whole seconds; defaults to the current time.
For saved keyed WAVs, supply the transmission epoch on reception, within
the search window. Without an explicit epoch, live operation uses the actual
transmit/capture start.
.TP
.BI \-\-search\-seconds " N"
Search epochs within N seconds on either side, nearest first;
0\(en32768, default 6.
.TP
.BI \-\-progress
Report timing search to standard error. With
.B listen \-\-json
also emit signal and preview events.
.SS Keys and resource limits
.TP
.BI \-\-keyfile " path"
Load symmetric keys. Both peers need the same key set and any bound pad.
Without a keyfile, operation is unencrypted.
.TP
.BI \-\-key\-name " name"
Select a named key set; default the first.
.B listen
without this option tries all sets in the keyfile on reception.
.TP
.BI \-\-key\-names " list"
Comma-separated names to create with
.BR keygen ;
default
.BR Default .
.TP
.BI \-\-pad " path"
Bind a keyfile to an external pad at creation, or supply its bound pad at load.
The pad must be larger than 1 GiB and remains a separate file.
.TP
.BI \-\-memory\-mb " N"
Batch PCM workspace, 1\(en4096 MiB; default 256.
.TP
.BI \-\-cache\-mb " N"
Source input and received-content limit, 1\(en4096 MiB; default 256.
.TP
.BI \-\-dsp\-mb " N"
Streaming DSP workspace, 1\(en1024 MiB; default 64.
These separate limits are not a total process memory cap.
.SS Recovery
These options apply to
.BR rx ,
.B simulate
and
.BR listen .
Additional hard-bit recovery begins only after physical completion.
.TP
.BI \-\-recovery\-seconds " N"
Recovery time budget, 0\(en86400 seconds; default 300. Zero disables it.
.TP
.BI \-\-recovery\-threads " N"
Recovery workers, 0\(en1024; default 0 selects available CPU cores.
.TP
.BI \-\-recovery\-bits " N"
Retained hard-bit slots, 1024\(en1048576; default 65536.
Separate from the displayed raw-bit prefix.
.TP
.BI \-\-recovery\-errors " N"
Reed\(enSolomon capacity reserved for additional byte errors, 0\(en24; default 2.
.SS Audio and simulation
.TP
.BI \-\-device " id"
Audio endpoint from
.BR devices .
Use
.B default
for the system default.
.TP
.B \-\-right\-mono
Transmit on the right channel instead of the default left channel.
A mono device uses its sole channel.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-mono
Transmit on both stereo channels. Conflicts with
.BR \-\-right\-mono .
.TP
.BI \-\-device\-type " audio"
Select analog audio, the only implemented device type.
.TP
.BI \-\-seconds " N"
For live
.BR rx ,
recording duration; default 15 seconds.
For
.BR listen ,
wall-clock run limit, 0\(en86400 seconds; default 0 means continuous.
Stopping a capture does not complete a reception.
.TP
.BI \-\-tx\-delay " N"
Delay after live transmission, 6\(en3600 seconds; default 6.
Automatically extended when the symbol-absence interval requires more time.
.TP
.BI \-\-snr " dB"
Simulated sample-power signal/noise ratio; default 20. For
.B simulate
only; mutually exclusive with a simulation preset.
.TP
.BI \-\-simulation " preset"
Link preset for
.BR simulate ,
.B listen
or
.BR analyze-link .
Quote the two-part name. Presets are
.B "3dBm \-6dB"
and 3dBm at \-60, \-90, \-120, \-170, \-200 or \-230dB;
50dBm at \-200 or \-270dB; and 70dBm at \-250dB.
In
.BR listen ,
.B no
or
.B off
selects live audio.
.TP
.BI \-\-seed " N"
Simulation or statistical-analysis seed; default 1.
.TP
.BI \-\-delay\-samples " N"
Initial sampled-channel delay for
.B simulate
or the assumed delay for
.BR analyze-link ;
default 137.
.TP
.BI \-\-frequency\-offset " Hz"
Frequency offset for
.B simulate
or
.BR analyze-link ;
default 0.
.TP
.BI \-\-receiver\-time " seconds"
Independent receive epoch for
.BR simulate ;
default the transmit epoch.
.TP
.BI \-\-oscillator " model"
Baseband model for bounded receiver search and simulated impairments:
.B crystal
(default),
.BR gpsdo-xo ,
.B gpsdo-tcxo
or
.BR gpsdo-ocxo .
Does not control hardware.
.TP
.BI \-\-rf\-oscillator " model"
Shift model; same choices, default crystal. At Shift 0 all of its frequency and
phase contributions are excluded, regardless of the reference setting.
For a legacy positive-Shift shared reference, this flag selects the shared model.
.TP
.BI \-\-reference " independent|shared-radio"
Independent Baseband and Shift references (default), or one shared sampling/mixer
reference for a positive Shift. A positive shared Shift uses the rf-oscillator
profile once for both effects; Shift 0 uses only the oscillator/Baseband profile.
.B \-\-lf\-reference 0
is a legacy shared-reference shorthand, unrelated to setting Shift to 0 Hz.
.TP
.BI \-\-search\-margin " N"
Multiply declared frequency and clock accuracy bounds; default 3, minimum 1.
The margin does not multiply simulated impairments.
.TP
.BI \-\-clock\-error\-ppm " N"
Override signed simulated relative clock error; crystal default 100 ppm.
This changes channel truth without widening the declared receiver bounds.
.TP
.BI \-\-phase\-noise " N"
Override phase diffusion in degrees per square root second;
crystal default 0.5.
.SS Statistical link analysis
The following options apply only to
.BR analyze-link .
.TP
.BI \-\-tx\-dbm " N"
.TQ
.BI \-\-attenuation\-db " N"
Transmit power and nonpositive channel attenuation. Supply both, or use
.BR \-\-simulation .
.TP
.BI \-\-noise\-figure\-db " N"
Receiver noise figure; default 10 dB.
.TP
.BI \-\-symbol\-seconds " N"
Override the analyzed symbol duration; default the transmit plan.
.TP
.BI \-\-coherent\-seconds " N"
Maximum coherent segment; default 3600 seconds.
.TP
.BI \-\-trials " N"
Monte Carlo trials per reference model, 1\(en1000000; default 10000.
.TP
.BI \-\-hypotheses " N"
Searched alternatives, including both bits; default 1000000.
.TP
.BI \-\-false\-alarm " P"
Global reference false-alarm budget; default 0.000001.
.TP
.BI \-\-residual\-frequency\-hz " N"
Frequency error after hypothetical acquisition; default 0.
.TP
.BI \-\-template\-correlation " N"
Assumed normalized template correlation; default 0.
.SS General
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print command help and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the application version and exit.
.SH RECEPTION
Nonempty text of 1\(en16 source bytes uses a fixed short dictionary.
Short text and explicit bit strings have no header, transmitted length,
padding, error correction or MAC. Longer text and all attachments use fixed
128-coded-byte intervals, each preceded by a 192-bit marker.
.PP
Only observed signal absence ends reception. Consecutive fully scored absent
symbols must cover six seconds; a long symbol must finish before it can be
classified absent. EOF, cancellation, successful decoding and authentication
do not complete a stream. Generated WAVs include quiet tail samples;
truncated input WAVs do not acquire an artificial tail.
.PP
Newly accepted bits appear on the next progress poll. The diagnostic prefix
retains at most 4096 raw bits; counts can continue beyond it. Missing slots
are zero placeholders, not observed zero bits. Recovery status is separate
from physical completion.
.SH OUTPUT
Text reception writes restricted ASCII to standard output. Letters, digits,
comma, period, @, space, hyphen, underscore, slash, equals and newline are
preserved; other received bytes are shown as underscores. Received filenames
use the same restriction. Use
.B rx \-\-save
for original bytes. Attachments are not saved automatically.
Diagnostics go to standard error.
.PP
With
.BR \-\-json ,
inspect
.BR stream_complete ,
.BR content_validated ,
.B short_text_decoded
and
.B authenticated
separately. Decoded short text is not authenticated.
.B estimate
and
.B analyze-link
always produce JSON.
.PP
.B listen \-\-json
produces one JSON object per line. Track each
.B signal_id
at its latest
.BR revision ;
clear the previous interpretation on revision and remove identities in
.BR superseded_ids .
A later receive profile may revise a completed interpretation back to pending.
.B reception_update
links an interpretation's
.B reception_id
to a completed payload's
.BR id .
.SH EXAMPLES
Simulate a short message:
.PP
.nf
.RS
pump simulate \-\-text 'CQ hello' \-\-snr 12 \-\-json
.RE
.fi
.PP
Estimate a transmission, then send and receive a file using a fixed epoch:
.PP
.nf
.RS
pump estimate \-\-input note.txt
pump tx \-\-input note.txt \-\-time 1800000000 \e
    \-\-output transfer.wav
pump rx \-\-input transfer.wav \-\-time 1800000000 \e
    \-\-save received.txt
.RE
.fi
.PP
Receive live audio, or send on a separate invocation:
.PP
.nf
.RS
pump listen \-\-device default \-\-json
pump tx \-\-text 'hello' \-\-device default
.RE
.fi
.PP
Create and inspect a shared keyfile:
.PP
.nf
.RS
pump keygen \-\-output shared.key \-\-key\-names Home,Portable
pump keys \-\-keyfile shared.key
.RE
.fi
.PP
Add the same
.B \-\-keyfile shared.key \-\-key\-name Home
to both ends of an encrypted transfer.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Command finished. This alone does not prove successful reception;
check the JSON completion and validation fields.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid arguments, input/output failure or another reported error.
.SH FILES
Input, output, keyfile and pad paths are explicit. Received content is retained
in bounded memory; no receive disk cache is created. Output and save commands
refuse to overwrite existing files.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B ALSA_PLUGIN_DIR
ALSA plugin directory for Linux live audio. An explicit value takes precedence
over portable-bundle host-plugin discovery.
.SH NOTES
Keep keyed peers' clocks within the configured search window. Do not reuse a
key and transmit schedule position: this can reveal relationships between
plaintexts and permits replay. Interval authentication does not authenticate
an intended whole-stream length.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pump-fast (1),
.BR datapump-gui (1)
